    {"claim": "The mandate itself is the capture surface — whoever drafts the audit standard decides what counts as adequate, and that drafting table fills up with the companies being audited.", "targets": [], "relationship": ""},
    {"claim": "Federal officials are actively moving to dismantle disparate-impact liability under Title VII and the Fair Housing Act, so discovery becomes the last lever a victim has.", "targets": [], "relationship": ""},
    {"claim": "The entire value of this statute lives in a variable the resolution leaves blank: whether independent, non-vendor third parties define audit adequacy.", "targets": [], "relationship": ""}
  ]
